## Latest Probe Comparison

| Variant | n | delta_y_mean | lowfreq_y_mae | rgb_mae | nonedge_hf_ratio | strong_edge_ratio | green_excess_delta | chroma_std_delta |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Deploy | 42 | 0.215 | 0.245 | 2.369 | 0.702 | 0.944 | -0.065 | -0.017 |
| NAFNet e71 last | 42 | -6.619 | 6.757 | 7.472 | 0.915 | 0.984 | -0.502 | -0.194 |
| Restormer e1 last | 42 | 1.500 | 1.517 | 2.078 | 0.983 | 0.978 | -0.933 | -0.132 |

## Interpretation

- Deploy:
  - Strongest flat/non-edge denoise.
  - Also the strongest smoothing/detail suppression.
  - Useful as production baseline but not ideal Teacher target if preserving texture/detail is important.
- NAFNet e71:
  - Better edge/detail preservation than Deploy.
  - Still carries visible global tone-down risk, especially `road_shaded` and `building`.
  - Current best Teacher candidate, but tone gate must remain active.
- Restormer e1:
  - Tone-safe direction appears safer for luma.
  - Too early to judge as Teacher because output remains close to RAW and denoise effect is weak.

