## Next

1. Keep NAFNet and Restormer live unless GPU scheduling or OOM requires intervention.
2. Re-run the same 42-frame probe when NAFNet reaches epoch 80 or 100.
3. Re-run the same 42-frame probe when Restormer tone-safe reaches a meaningful checkpoint, at least epoch 3 and preferably epoch 10.
4. For NAFNet, gate Teacher acceptance on both detail preservation and luma drift.
5. If NAFNet remains below about `-3` mean Y shift on the fixed probe, prepare a separate tone-safe NAFNet fine-tune instead of overwriting the current run.
6. Do not start MTKD Student training until Teacher outputs pass the real MC-G105 probe gates.
